#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# alphabetic_order

#% text
# `alphabetic_order(a, b)` gives 1, 0 or -1 as the strings `a` and `b` are in alphabetic order, equal or not: letter case is folded first, then lower case comes before upper case. `alphabetic_order()` and `alphabetic_order("English")` are the ordering function itself, for `sort`. Other languages' collations are not available.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
alphabetic_order("cat", "Cat")
#% output
#= 1

#% cell
alphabetic_order("fish", "cat")
#% output
#= -1

#% cell
sort(["cat", "fish", "catfish", "Cat"], alphabetic_order())
#% output
#= ["cat", "Cat", "catfish", "fish"]

